TASK-AETHER-LANE-SENDER|owner=acer|for=aether-claude|json=0

STEP 0 (host parity): acer just pushed the canonical v6 8byte-host.sh +
restart-8byte-host.sh to /sdcard/Asolaria. Adopt v6 now:
    sh /sdcard/Asolaria/restart-8byte-host.sh
Confirm it is running:
    pgrep -f 8byte-host.sh

GOAL: Build a SH tool (NO node, NO json) that lets THIS phone push an HBP envelope
to ANY host:port on the fabric -- phone-to-phone OR phone-to-acer-bus.

WRITE THIS FILE: /sdcard/Asolaria/aether-lane-sender.sh

USAGE:  sh aether-lane-sender.sh <target_ip> <port> <EVT-TYPE> <short-msg>

BEHAVIOR:
  - SER=$(getprop ro.serialno); ts=$(date +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S)
  - Compose ONE HBP line:   <EVT-TYPE>|ts=$ts|host=$SER|msg=<short-msg>|json=0
  - If <port> is 4947 (the acer bus), send it as an HTTP POST to /behcs/send-hbp:
      body=the HBP line; send a raw  POST /behcs/send-hbp HTTP/1.1  with
      Host, Content-Type: text/plain, Content-Length: <byte-len of body>, Connection: close,
      blank line, then the body. Pipe to  nc -w 5 <ip> 4947 .
  - Otherwise (phone-to-phone receiver): send the raw line:
      printf '%s\n' "$line" | nc -w 5 <ip> <port>
  - Print the raw reply you get back. NO json. NO node.

SELF-TEST (actually run these, paste the real output, do not fake):
  1. Phone-to-phone -> Falcon's receiver:
       sh /sdcard/Asolaria/aether-lane-sender.sh 192.168.1.7 8801 EVT-AETHER-HELLO from-aether
     Show the EVT-LANE-ACK you get back.
  2. Phone-to-acer-bus:
       sh /sdcard/Asolaria/aether-lane-sender.sh 192.168.1.50 4947 EVT-AETHER-HELLO from-aether
     Show the HTTP response (a 200 with an hbp_ack row = success).

REPORT: Confirm Falcon ACKed (phone-to-phone fabric lane is LIVE) and report exactly
what acer's bus returned. Report honestly -- if something failed, say so.
